From 0a242d9c4071c01b99b6110d61ff85eeb2a82f90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luc3as <luc3as@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 17:01:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/25] Announce a listing again when its price drops
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Vinted sellers cut prices constantly, and a jacket that was too dear on
Monday may not be on Thursday — but once a listing had been announced it was
never mentioned again. Now the poller compares the prices of listings it
already knows against the page it just fetched, and when the total has fallen
by PRICE_DROP_MIN_PERCENT (default 10) it queues a "price drop" notification
carrying the old and new totals. This costs no additional requests: the
search's first page is fetched anyway and carries every listing's current
price, so a listing is tracked for as long as it stays on that page.

The outbox gains a kind ('new' or 'price_drop') and the previous price; its
unique key grows to include both, since a price can drop more than once,
which SQLite only allows by rebuilding the table (migration 0006). Every
sender shows the drop — Telegram and Discord headline it with old → new and
the percentage, ntfy changes the tag, the webhook payload gains additive
"event" and "previous_total_price" fields at the same contract version.
